.TH TR 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
tr \- translate or delete characters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tr
\fISET1\fR \fISET2\fR\n.br\n\fBtr \-d\fR \fISET1\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy standard input to standard output, translating characters in SET1 to the corresponding character in SET2 (or deleting them, with \fB\-d\fR). Sets are literal character lists; \fB[a\-z]\fR-style ranges are not supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Delete characters in SET1 instead of translating them.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
